  "result": "The gate returned **OK** for NRS_484B_253_o1 (7 witnesses), using 2 of the 6 runs.\n\n**What the rule says:**\n- **Who and when:** the subject must be a vehicle under DEF-NRS-484A-320, and the rule applies when it is in an intersection X and has `int.left_turn` declared at X.\n- **The vehicles it must yield to:**\n  - c1 is the approach lane the subject came in on.\n  - v is any other vehicle that came in on (or is still on) an approach c2 whose direction is roughly opposite c1's: the dot product is below −`p.oncoming_heading_cos`.\n  - v counts if it is inside X, or if it is still on c2 and in conflict with the subject. \"In conflict\" means their centres come within `p.conflict_centre_clearance` within `p.conflict_horizon`.\n- **The duty:** the subject must not touch v, and must not move faster than `p.halt_speed_tolerance` while in that conflict.\n\n**One choice the node didn't spell out:** the lane quantifiers also pick up the intersection itself, because it counts as a travel region. Core treats \"does this lane enter X\" as unknown for a region that isn't a lane, which would have turned the compliant witnesses into unknown. An intersection can't be an approach into itself, so I excluded X from both lane positions (`not (same c1 X)`, `not (same c2 X)`). I recorded this in the rule's header comment as a structural choice, not a narrowing, and declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses:** the six planned ones (`forbid`, `permit`, `idle`, `blind`, `branch_1`, `branch_2`) plus one I added. `branch_3` is a violation where the oncoming car is already inside the intersection and off its lane. It is the only witness that exercises the \"within the intersection\" case.\n\n**Two things outside the plan:**\n- My first gate run was on the untouched skeleton, which returned UNUSED_CLAIM. That run wasn't needed and used up one of the six.\n- Before that, I mistakenly tried the gate command with extra arguments (`--help` piped to `head`). The sandbox denied it and it never ran.\n\nThe full account is in `task_result.md` in the working directory.",
